Eidolon is a C++ tool built on top of MLIR/LLVM that is capable of verifying instances of lowered MLIR.

Eidolon is desirable when you must ensure that an instance of lowered MLIR refines the semantics of the source it was lowered from. Given an MLIR input, it lowers a copy with MLIR's own pass and verifies that the lowering refines the source.

As a proof of concept, Eidolon aims to support the warp-collective operations in the gpu dialect, and their lowerings to NVVM, ROCDL, and SPIR-V. There is currently partial support for gpu.shuffle lowered to NVVM.

The aim is to ensure the tool is extensible, at first within the gpu dialect, and ideally to other dialects in MLIR. 

Requirements:
  - LLVM 23.1.3
  - Z3
  - CMake 3.31 (or newer)
  - Ninja, clang, lld

Build:
  PATH=$LLVM/bin:$PATH cmake -G Ninja -S . -B build \
  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
  -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=clang -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=clang++ \
  -DMLIR_DIR=$LLVM/lib/cmake/mlir -DLLVM_USE_LINKER=lld
  ninja -C build

  With $LLVM set to the directory the LLVM release is unpacked in.

More documentation will follow.
